@@ -122,6 +122,61 @@ Error messages are split by audience. What a user sees is always Chinese: the fr
 
 What a developer or an MCP agent sees is unchanged: backend `detail` stays as-is in the API response and in the logs, and the full diagnostic — status, status text, the raw response body, and the `X-Request-Id` that correlates with `requests.jsonl` — is written to the DevTools console on every failed request, alongside the original text of any error the UI replaced with a generic message. So "it says I have no permission" is answered by reading the console's request id, not by guessing which check rejected it.
 
+### Private evaluation execution traces
+
+`app.core.evaluation_tracing` provides an optional in-memory capture for an
+explicit evaluation caller. It is disabled by default, uses only the Python
+standard library, and has no file, network, logging, or DeepEval dependency:
+
+```python
+from app.core.evaluation_tracing import capture_evaluation_trace, evaluation_span
+
+with capture_evaluation_trace() as capture:
+    with evaluation_span("sn.request", "agent", input=question,
+                         metadata={"stage": "request"}) as root:
+        response = submit_system_question(question)
+        root.set_output(response.answer)
+trace = capture.to_dict()
+```
+
+The caller owns the request root, artifact access controls, storage and retention.
+This is a **private contentful evaluation artifact**, separate from ordinary
+content-free telemetry: it includes selected questions, explicit observable
+plans/decisions, retrieved passages, actual synthesis context, provider-facing
+messages and returned answer content. It does not serialize clients, repositories,
+settings, credentials, service endpoints, exception text, embeddings, arbitrary
+knowledge payloads, or provider `reasoning_content`/hidden chain-of-thought.
+Plain JSON business values are copied when recorded; unsupported values create a
+capture error without changing or repeating the original operation.
+
+Schema `sn-execution-trace-v1` contains `trace_id`, `closed`, `spans`,
+`capture_errors`, and `duration_ms`. Each span has `span_id`, `parent_id`, `name`,
+`kind` (`agent`, `retriever`, `tool`, or `llm`), `input`, `output`, `metadata`,
+`status`, monotonic `start_time`/`end_time` in seconds, and `duration_ms`.
+Terminal status is `completed`, `error`, or `cancelled`; failures expose only
+`error_type`. A span still running at capture close retains `running` and creates
+`span_open_at_close`; it must not be treated as complete. Entry order is stable,
+but concurrent spans overlap: do not sum nested durations as elapsed wall time.
+Closed captures ignore late writes, nested captures restore their outer scope,
+and existing `copy_context()` workers retain the correct request and parent.
+
+Coverage is the synchronous native Ask call tree: intent preview, Ask dispatch,
+chunk retrieval, reasoning retrieval and its explicit initial plan/reflection,
+native search/graph/document/enumeration actions, chunk/mix/reasoning synthesis,
+and `OpenAICompatibleClient.chat_json`. Stage names are `intent`, `ask`,
+`retrieve`, `plan`, `reflect`, `action`, `synthesis`, and `llm`. Confirmed-intent
+plans are recorded as adopted plans rather than fabricated model calls. LLM spans
+represent a logical call including cache lookup and retries, not individual HTTP
+attempts. Model doubles/custom clients do not automatically produce LLM spans.
+State-mutating actions expose their selected outcome fields; graph payload text
+is captured through the actual synthesis context instead of arbitrary object
+serialization. Plugin actions mark `coverage=call_boundary_only` and
+`downstream_internals_traced=false`; detached work, plugin services, streaming
+transport, and external daemons are not claimed as fully traced. Inline control
+decisions such as outline updates remain observable in reflection outputs, not
+independent action spans. A successful answer does not prove complete capture;
+check coverage, `closed`, unfinished spans, and `capture_errors` separately.
+
